{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794222368,"nonce":"i3VUyL1JH0oEPMLNoa3X0BTuOEI=","title":"jno.fdm nonlinear march drops the lagged-Jacobian Newton default","message":"With a linear= slot, _run_block sets nonlinear = nonlinear or jno.solve.newton(direct=True), an explicit Newton with a fresh tangent and factorization every iteration. The documented default of a transient march is newton(reuse=True) (lagged Jacobian), which keeps the factorization across iterations and steps with lu(backend='cudss' | 'pardiso'). A warm bdf2 march of a 32x32 Brusselator made 212 sparse LU calls for 100 steps. Open question: make reuse=True the fdm default too, as fem.solve does.","files":null}]}